Z||000000||Patrick||11-22-1999||02:06 PM||||<BR>Cliff, is there any way that everyone could have some control as to what page opens on a mutiple page thread. For any one who is new to the forum, obviously they'd want a thread to open on the first page. However, for those of us who check in every day (or more often), it would be nice to have the threads open on the latest page instead.<P>Any chance that UBB would support something like that?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||11-22-1999||04:11 PM||||Well, it supports one or the other... It either show the oldest messages first (as it is now), or the last messages first. Unfortunately this is not user controlled.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Patrick||11-23-1999||02:31 AM||||<BR>Cliff, when you say that UBB can show the latest messages first, do you mean having ALL the posts listed in reverse order? If that's what you mean, that's a horrible way to have the posts listed. The current way is much better.<P>I was just hoping that there was some user defined method of having the latest <B>page</B> displayed, but retaining the <B>posts</B> in same order as they are now on that page.<P>Sounds like it's not possible. Oh well...||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-23-1999||08:02 PM||||I believe it's an administrative setting only, and the setting is global. There is no user control(no UBB/HTML). It's been awhile since I looked at the ultimate "manual".||||reg||1
